prompt_template:
Use case: ads-marketing. Create one finished full-bleed illustrated community-event poster in {ASPECT_RATIO}. It must stand alone as a complete raster design. Apply the following visual system in priority order:
{STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS}
New scene and action: {SUBJECT_ACTION}
Design intention: {DESIGN_DIRECTION}
Use only the plan matching the requested ratio. Landscape 16:9 plan: {LANDSCAPE_PLAN}
Portrait 9:16 plan: {PORTRAIT_PLAN}
Exact visible text, with no other wording: main headline "{MAIN_TEXT}"; short italic display-serif phrase "{SECONDARY_TEXT}"; event information "{EVENT_DETAILS}". Preserve all words and numbers; line breaks and separator dots may change. Make the headline bold black grotesk, subtitle black italic serif and details readable black sans-serif. Compose type and scene together, with calm red space and a few thin organizing rules only where useful. Background warm vermilion #E84125, near-black #080807 ink; red interiors of figures remain the same red as the ground. Broad blunt irregular marker/brush outlines, simple dot/curved eyes, oval ring noses, smiles and mitten hands. Keep occasional dry terminals at stroke scale and small dense irregular black stippling or broken checks only in one or two garment/textile regions; ground stays nearly clean. Everything is flat ink without a light source. Replace these source-specific elements completely:
{SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID}
No white or pale fills, no gradients, no 3D, no photographic detail, no slick vector finish, no globally distressed paper, no watermarks or brand emblems. Do not let illustration strokes obscure required wording.
